course: dictionary
lesson: 4168
title: Gob: a word with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one. «Bit of a gob on him, mind» means the person talks too much, so a gob here is a mouth. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: Gob is slang, which means informal everyday talk, and in «shut your gob» it is rude. Use it with friends or in a story, but not with teachers or grown-ups in polite talk. Use your mouth or be quiet instead.
explain: Gob can also mean a lump or blob of something soft and wet, or «gobs» of something, which means a lot of it. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Gob is slang, and in «shut your gob» it means your mouth and is rude.
fact: «Gobsmacked» means amazed or very surprised.
fact: A «gobstopper» is a very big, hard sweet.
fact: A «gob of spit» or «a gob of glue» is a lump or blob of something soft and wet.
fact: «Gobs of» something means a lot of it, as in «gobs of money».
exercise: «Shut your gob!» What does gob mean here? | *Mouth | Hat | Shoe | Sweet
exercise: «There was a gob of glue on the paper.» What is a gob of glue? | A long thin line | A small tin | *A lump or blob | A clean sheet of paper
exercise: Dad says he was «gobsmacked» by the news. What does he mean? | Sleepy | Bored | Angry with the cook | *Amazed
test: «We have gobs of time to finish the project.» What does gobs of mean? | None at all | Gold coins | A few | *A lot of
test: Why should you not say «shut your gob» to your teacher? | *It is rude slang | It means please | It is a kind word | It is the word for a sweet
exam: Which word means a very big, hard sweet? | Toffee | Biscuit | *Gobstopper | Lollipop
